A Stupid Ascension Trick Ascension Post for a simple one this time -
Stupid Ascension Trick 23.1.1: "Never advanced any skill".

This is probably one of the easier stupid tricks that I put in the list
(http://thinksystem.net/nethack). Of course, I also tried it with the
easiest role/race I could think of: a dwarven valkyrie. Dwarf for the
infravision and less hostility in the Mines, Valkyrie for the starting
Basic skill in longswords (which are a bit over-represented in the list
of good artifact weapons) and the excellent quest artifact. If someone
wants to do an unenhanced Healer or Tourist, they would have a lot
more to crow about.

It was a fairly uneventful game. Useful items (speed boots, magic
whistle, magic lamp) showed up pretty early and there were not any
really scary moments. If I was willing to be a bit more patient or take
more risks, I probably could have added wishless and polyless to the
genocideless that this game had. If I remember correctly the wishes
went for a ring of levitation and three magic markers. I could have
managed everything except for the Plane of Air without the ring of
levitation without too much trouble. (What is the best way to deal with
the Plane if you don't use a ring or boots? Quaff a blessed potion?
Ride a flying mount or polymorph into something like a Vampire Lord?)
The magic markers were almost entirely used to improve my armor class,
but with the Orb of Fate and the dozen or so potions of full healing
that I walked out with, I probably did not need it as low as it was.

I did do some poly-piling, but I don't recall anything useful coming
out of it, so I probably could have avoided that also.

