Longsword was the only one I really used. I may have thrown a couple
of daggers, but mostly it was close-in work. I got enough hits in
with the pick-axe to be eligible to improve it just because I was
too lazy to swap to a sword to deal with a low-level monster while
I was in the middle of tunneling.

I didn't take notes on this one, but there was an amusing (to me) bit
that could be a stupid trick on its own: Before going to explore the
deep depths and find the vibrating square I decided to collect up
some domestic animals and run them through a polymorph trap to see if
I could get some good help. I got a Rock Troll, Vampire, and Lich (all
which are nice) and a Woodchuck. I thought it would be cool to ascend
with the woodchuck and so kept it around. It went fine for quite a few
levels (who knew that woodchucks tunneled? I didn't at least) until
the zoo level of the wizard's tower. An Umber Hulk confused the Lich
and it killed off Chucky the woodchuck. Oh well.


